       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose looks like an error.\n\n**Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day.** That is double the maximum labeled daily dose:\n- Immediate-release maximum: 2,550 mg/day. Doses are usually 500\u20131,000 mg per administration, and no more than 850 mg three times daily.\n- Extended-release maximum: 2,000\u20132,500 mg/day.\n\nA dose this high raises the risk of serious lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the IR maximum)\n- **1000 mg PO twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **500 mg or 1000 mg** at some other frequency\n- **1700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily\n\nIf you do want 1700 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
